{
  "Files chosen with a button or dropped on the box, listed with their size and what happens to them: uploaded as they come, on a button or programmatically, with progress, cancel, retry and remove on each. Files outside the limits are listed with the reason.": "",
  "Choosing, dropping, uploading": "",
  "`upload` is your own way to send a file: report progress, stop on the signal, resolve to the response. With `uploadUrl` instead, the uploader sends the file itself, in one piece or in chunks (`chunkSize`).": "",
  "When files go up": "",
  "Sending to a server": "",
  "The uploader posts a form with the file in `uploadField` (`file` by default) to `uploadUrl`, with `uploadHeaders`; a 2xx answer is the item’s `response`, JSON parsed when it is JSON. With `chunkSize` each piece carries `Content-Range` and the fields `chunkIndex` and `chunkCount`.": "",
  "The button opens the file dialog; files may be dropped on the box too, which lights up while they are over it.": "",
  "A file outside `accept`, the sizes or `maxFiles` is listed as refused with the reason, and is not in the value.": "",
  "As chosen, on the Upload button, or programmatically. A row shows the progress and a Cancel button meanwhile; afterwards “Uploaded”, or the failure with Retry. The server’s answer is the item’s `response` (JSON parsed).": "",
  "With `chunkSize` the file goes in pieces, each a request with `Content-Range: bytes start-end/total`; progress runs over the whole.": "",
  "Each row has a remove button; a running upload is stopped first.": "",
  "The select button is the field’s control: the label marks it, Space and Enter open the dialog.": "",
  "A list of rows: the name, the size and the state as text; the progress bar named after the file; the buttons named “Cancel the upload of …”, “Retry”, “Remove …”.": "",
  "The reasons a file was refused and the failures speak in the kit language, or in the server’s words.": "",
  "The field. `data-dragover` while files are over it.": "",
  "The select button, the hint, the Upload button.": "",
  "The list and each row. `data-status` on the row.": "",
  "Units: the box with files over it, the two buttons (`hover`, `pressed`, `focus`, `disabled`), the hint, the list, a row per status, the file glyph, the texts.": "",
  "Places: the field’s box as a drop zone (a dashed frame, its corners, its padding); the row’s buttons.": "",
  "The spaces in the box, in a button and in a row.": "",
  "The files taken (the refused ones are not in it). `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Several files at once; `false` keeps one, the newest.": "",
  "What may be chosen, as for `<input type=\"file\">`: `.png,.jpg`, `image/*`, `application/pdf`.": "",
  "Bytes. A file outside is listed as refused, with the reason.": "",
  "How many files may be taken in all.": "",
  "Files may be dropped on the box.": "",
